course: dictionary
lesson: 10350
title: Light and materials
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Materials are the things objects are made of, like glass, wood and plastic. Some let light through and some do not. Scientists sort materials into three groups: transparent, translucent and opaque. Translucent is the middle group.
explain: «Transparent materials let light through, translucent ones let some through, and opaque ones block it.» Clear glass lets all the light through, so you see sharp shapes. Wood lets none through. Translucent materials sit between these two.
explain: With a translucent material, light gets through, but you cannot see clearly through it. Shapes behind it look blurry or faded. «Frosted glass is translucent» because you can see light and rough shadows through it, but not the details.
fact: Translucent means letting some light pass through, but you cannot see clearly through it.
fact: Examples of translucent things are tracing paper, frosted glass, a thin leaf and some plastic.
fact: Transparent means clear, so you can see through it. Opaque means no light gets through.
fact: Scientists use the words transparent, translucent and opaque when they sort materials by how much light they let through.
exercise: «Frosted glass is translucent.» What does translucent mean? | Lets no light through at all | *Lets some light pass through, but you cannot see clearly through it | Gives out its own light like a bulb | Lets all the light through, so you see everything sharply
exercise: Which of these is translucent? | Clear window glass | Metal spoon | *Frosted glass | Wood
exercise: «Transparent materials let light through, translucent ones let some through, and opaque ones block it.» Which word means light is blocked completely? | Transparent | Clear | Translucent | *Opaque
test: A thin leaf held up to the sun lets some light through, but you cannot see clearly through it. Which word describes it? | Opaque | *Translucent | Solid | Transparent
test: Clear glass lets you see through it perfectly. Which word describes it? | Opaque | *Transparent | Frosted | Translucent
exam: Tracing paper lets some light through, but everything behind it looks blurry. Which word describes it? | Transparent | Opaque | *Translucent
